EVALUATION.md §1, TYPES.md §1, DECISIONS 209: a broken check is part of its record's body, so it
breaks the record and every value typed by it: `heavy` is neither evaluated nor checked, nor is
`gemDiv`, which reads it; W4001 at Gem counts `heavy` only (DECISIONS 331). A broken method breaks only its callers: `box` is still checked (E5001)
and `other` still evaluated (E4102) while `viaMethod` stays silent.
-- check-only --
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Gem.
record Gem {
  /// Weight.
  weight: Int

  check light: weight < 5 else "heavy"

  check broken: weight < "5" else "broken"
}

/// Fails light, but Gem is broken.
let heavy: Gem = { weight: 9 }

/// Reads heavy.
let gemDiv: Int = heavy.weight / 0

/// Box.
record Box {
  /// N.
  n: Int

  check small: n < 10 else "big"

  /// Broken method.
  fn twice() -> Int { return n * "2" }
}

/// Fails small.
let box: Box = { n: 20 }

/// Calls the broken method.
let viaMethod: Int = box.twice() / 0

/// Unrelated.
let other: Int = box.n / 0
-- select --
a
-- findings.txt --
warning[W4001]  a/a.canon:5:8
  1 value was not evaluated or checked because a.Gem is broken: fix the errors in it or in the types it names

error[E3310]  a/a.canon:11:17
  < needs an orderable type, found String

error[E3007]  a/a.canon:28:30
  operator * is not defined for Int and String

error[E5001]  a/a.canon:32:16
  box: big
  expected by a/a.canon:25 (check small)

error[E4102]  a/a.canon:38:18
  other: division by zero

4 errors, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
